                <pb facs="0692" n="580" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg580"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 033.1211/25</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Fletcher</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-11T15:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 11, 1918, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1168. In an interview with President Carranza this morning I asked him his
                    impression of the President’s speech to the Mexican journalists. He answered
                    with a smile that it was very good and that he hoped it would be corroborated by
                    subsequent events and added that he had nothing more to say. I read to him the
                    last draft of the President’s Pan American treaty plan<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d547-f1"/> referred to in the speech, and explained the causes which
                    prevented its realization at the time proposed, and told him that the President
                    hoped to be able to secure its adoption later. He said he had read something of
                    it and seemed favorably disposed toward it.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fletcher</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
